  <article class="rules-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Micro Space Empire v.93</p>
    <h1>How to play</h1>
    <p>Survive two years and earn victory points from controlled systems, researched technologies, exploration, science, and complete conquest.</p>
    <h2>Turn sequence</h2>
    <ol><li><strong>Explore, Conquer, or Bide Time.</strong> Exploration always leads to an attack. Roll a d6 plus Military against Resistance.</li><li><strong>Collect.</strong> Gain production up to your storage cap. If you have Interspecies Commerce, you may then make one trade.</li><li><strong>Build.</strong> Build Military once and research one Technology, in either order.</li><li><strong>Event.</strong> Reveal and resolve the next event card.</li></ol>
    <h2>Limits and technologies</h2>
    <p>Resources and Military normally cap at 3. Interstellar Banking raises resource storage to 5; Capital Ships raises Military to 5. Technologies on the right side of each pair require the technology immediately to their left.</p>
    <h2>Years and scoring</h2>
    <p>Year 1 contains seven events. All enabled events are reshuffled and six are selected for Year 2. After the sixth Year 2 event, score controlled systems, one point per technology, one point for exploring every selected system, one point for all technologies, and three points for controlling every selected system.</p>
    <h2>Digital expansion rulings</h2>
    <p>Meteor Storms suppress only the targeted system’s production for two collections. Expansion events use the base Home World protections, and Alien Diplomatic Mission cannot exceed the current Military cap.</p>
    <p class="muted">General rules follow the supplied v.93 rulebook. Card-specific values follow the original v.92 cards and supplied five-card expansion.</p>
  </article>
</main>
